WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.750
- So President Trump is
now former president Trump

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.270
and Joe Biden is now the current President

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.470
of the United States.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.870
And as many have pointed out

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:10.968
that means that Donald Trump
is now a private citizen.

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:12.500
So to whatever extent

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.038
that president Trump had
immunity as president,

00:00:15.038 --> 00:00:16.673
that no longer applies.

00:00:16.673 --> 00:00:18.471
And as a private citizen,

00:00:18.471 --> 00:00:22.067
Trump can now be sued
and investigated for all

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.560
of the things that he
may or may not have done.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.393
And there were a lot

00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:26.990
of open questions as President.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.530
Can a sitting president be indicted?

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.530
Can they be investigated?

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.831
Can they apply executive
privilege whenever they want?

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.630
And you'd think as a private citizen

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.230
a lot of those questions
would be answered.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.459
But the truth is there are a
lot of open questions still.

00:00:37.459 --> 00:00:39.910
If and when former President
Trump is investigated,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.930
he will claim some sort
of residual immunity.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.660
And these are still questions
that will have to be litigated

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.380
and answered by the courts

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.960
for any of these
investigations to go forward.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.441
Because this wasn't a normal presidency

00:00:51.441 --> 00:00:53.234
and he wasn't a normal president.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.832
So stay tuned for more
presidential legal news.

00:00:55.832 --> 00:00:56.810
And as always,

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.283
I'll see you in court.

